{"name":"Lottery Winnings","hex":"#768371","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lottery","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A scheme for the distribution of prizes by lot or chance, especially a gaming scheme in which one or more tickets bearing particular numbers draw prizes, the other tickets are blanks.","Something decided by chance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lottery"},{"term":"winnings","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of winning"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The spoils of a win; something, usually money, that has been won, usually by gambling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winnings"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lottery","blocks":[{"text":"A lottery is a form of gambling that involves the drawing of numbers at random for a prize. Some governments outlaw lotteries, while others endorse them to the extent of organizing a national or state lottery. It is common to find some degree of regulation of lottery by governments. The most common regulations are prohibition of sale to minors and licensing of ticket vendors. Although lotteries were common in the United States and some other countries during the 19th century, by the beginning of the 20th century, most forms of gambling, including lotteries and sweepstakes, were illegal in the U.S. and most of Europe as well as many other countries. This remained so until well after World War II. In the 1960s, casinos and lotteries began to re-appear throughout the world as a means for governments to raise revenue without raising taxes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Texas_Lottery_drawing.jpg/330px-Texas_Lottery_drawing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lottery","wikidata":"Q189409"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Lottery_tickets_for_sale%2C_Chandigarh.%2C_India._2910.jpg/500